# Landing / Page Image Quality

When editing user-facing pages or SCSS that include images:

## Sources
- No `placehold.co`, `via.placeholder.com`, `dummyimage.com`, `picsum.photos`, or broken hotlinks
- Prefer committed assets under classic `project-saral/assets/` or SPFx `src/webparts/**/assets/` / user-approved URLs
- Confirm license before third-party images
- Do not bundle large files under `assets/videos` unless the slice requires it

## Quality & CLS
- Real product imagery — not vague stock filler
- Explicit `width`/`height` or CSS `aspect-ratio` to prevent layout shift
- Prefer optimized sizes; lazy-load below-fold (`loading="lazy"`)

## Accessibility
- Informative images: specific `alt`
- Decorative: empty `alt`
- Do not put essential copy only inside an image

## Checks
- Paths resolve in this repo (classic `project-saral/assets/`, SPFx bundled assets, or property-pane URL)
- Mobile + desktop crop still readable
- Error/empty states must not show broken-image icons
